196
00:15:52,085 --> 00:15:57,304
Your assignment has four questions about one servo control box. One:

197
00:15:57,324 --> 00:15:58,845
in a 45-degree room,

198
00:15:58,865 --> 00:16:05,317
with an average loss of about 18 watts and about 8.3 watts per switch during starts,

199
00:16:05,337 --> 00:16:08,707
use the thermal network to find the box air,

200
00:16:08,727 --> 00:16:13,637
heat-sink and peak junction temperatures and the capacitor life,

201
00:16:13,657 --> 00:16:18,953
and check them against the 100-degree alarm and the 125-degree limit.

202
00:16:19,353 --> 00:16:23,392
Two: at 38 degrees with a lint blockage of 0.5,

203
00:16:23,412 --> 00:16:29,610
what is the largest clean heat-sink resistance that keeps the sink at or

204
00:16:29,630 --> 00:16:31,165
below 100 degrees?

205
00:16:31,185 --> 00:16:36,174
If the junction must also stay at or below 125, what then,

206
00:16:36,194 --> 00:16:38,937
and which constraint is tighter?

207
00:16:39,337 --> 00:16:43,797
Three uses the lab: at 45 degrees and 16 kilohertz,

208
00:16:43,817 --> 00:16:50,297
find the switching-time range that meets all three criteria and compare it

209
00:16:50,317 --> 00:16:54,161
with 235 to 470 nanoseconds at 12 kilohertz.

210
00:16:54,181 --> 00:16:59,168
Four is a discussion: boxes almost never fail in burn-in,

211
00:16:59,188 --> 00:17:04,614
yet first-year returns reach 2 percent. What could cause that,

212
00:17:04,634 --> 00:17:09,094
and how would you change the test and burn-in flow?

213
00:17:09,494 --> 00:17:13,073
